1
00:00:01,324 --> 00:00:13,165
(Q11（Matching）) So if you're one of those people who hasn't found the perfect physical activity yet - here are some things to think about which might help you make the right decision for you.

2
00:00:13,165 --> 00:00:18,963
The first question to ask yourself is whether you would enjoy training in a gym.

3
00:00:18,963 --> 00:00:31,561
Many people are put off by the idea of having to fit a visit to the gym into their busy day - you often have to go very early or late as some gyms can get very crowded.

4
00:00:31,561 --> 00:00:37,851
[Q11答案句（F） 解释型 短时间内看到效果 = fast results] But with regular training you'll see a big difference in a relatively short space of time.

5
00:00:37,851 --> 00:00:42,452
(Q12) Running has become incredibly popular in recent years.

6
00:00:42,452 --> 00:00:53,759
[Q12答案句（D） accessible + anyone can run = fitness level unimportant] That's probably got a lot to do with the fact that it's a very accessible form of exercise - anyone can run - even if you can only run a few metres to begin with.&nbsp;

7
00:00:53,759 --> 00:01:01,609
But make sure you get the right shoes - it's worth investing in a high quality pair and they don't come cheap.

8
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:11,250
[Q12干扰项A： 不取决于天气， 听到 do it any time of the day 就选A， 错❌] Another great thing about running is that you can do it at any time of day or night - the only thing that may stop you is snow and ice.

9
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:15,693
(Q13) Swimming is another really good way to build fitness.

10
00:01:15,693 --> 00:01:22,554
[Q13答案句： A， not dependent on season] What attracts many people is that you can swim in an indoor pool at any time of year.

11
00:01:22,554 --> 00:01:30,473
On the other hand, it can be quite boring or solitary - it's hard to chat to people while you're swimming lengths.

12
00:01:30,473 --> 00:01:35,002
(Q14) Cycling has become almost as popular as running in recent years.

13
00:01:35,002 --> 00:01:51,121
[Q14答案句（B） fun = enjoyable] That's probably because as well as improving their fitness, many people say being out in the fresh air in a park or in the countryside can be fun, provided the conditions are right, of course - only fanatics go out in the wind and rain!

14
00:01:51,121 --> 00:01:59,877
(Q15) Yoga is a good choice for those of you looking for exercise which focuses on developing both a healthy mind and body.

15
00:01:59,877 --> 00:02:09,362
[Q15答案句（C）： 否定含义， less chance of getting hurt = low risk， hurt =injury 但不重点提这个] It's a good way of building strength and with the right instructor, there's less chance of hurting yourself than with other more active sports.

16
00:02:09,362 --> 00:02:17,963
But don't expect to find it easy - it can be surprisingly challenging, especially for people who aren't very flexible.

17
00:02:17,963 --> 00:02:22,866
(Q16) Getting a personal trainer is a good way to start your fitness programme.

18
00:02:22,866 --> 00:02:27,130
Obviously there can be significant costs involved.

19
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:34,946
[Q16答案句G：解释 encourage + less likely to give up = motivating] But if you've got someone there to encourage you and help you achieve your goals, you're less likely to give up.

20
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:42,477
Make sure you get someone with a recognised qualification, though, or you could do yourself permanent damage.

21
00:02:42,477 --> 00:02:48,485
(Q17&18（多选）) Whatever you do, don't join a gym unless you're sure you'll make good use of it.

22
00:02:48,485 --> 00:02:55,542
So many people waste lots of money by signing up for membership and then hardly ever go.

23
00:02:55,542 --> 00:02:58,513
What happens to their good intentions?

24
00:02:58,513 --> 00:03:06,566
I don't think people suddenly stop caring about improving their fitness, or decide they have more important things to do.

25
00:03:06,566 --> 00:03:13,037
I think people lose interest when they don't think they're making enough progress.

26
00:03:13,037 --> 00:03:19,344
That's when they give up hope and stop believing they'll ever achieve their goals.

27
00:03:19,344 --> 00:03:34,990
Also, what people sometimes don't realise when they start is that it takes a lot of determination and hard work to keep training week after week and lots of people don't have that kind of commitment.

28
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:44,559
(Q19&20) One thing you can do to help yourself is to set manageable goals - be realistic and don't push yourself too far.

29
00:03:44,559 --> 00:03:50,958
Some people advise writing goals down, but I think it's better to have a flexible approach.

30
00:03:50,958 --> 00:03:53,458
Give yourself a really nice treat every time you reach one of your goals. And don't get too upset if you experience setbacks - it's a journey - there are bound to be difficulties along the way.

